<article class="env-definition" id="0EDX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EDX">Definition <span data-tag="0EDX">82.2.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> for any good $X/B$ and any irreducible closed subset $T \subset |X|$ we define </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _\delta (T) = \delta (\xi )  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\xi \in T$ is the generic point of $T$. We will call this the <em>$\delta $-dimension of $T$</em>. If $T \subset |X|$ is any closed subset, then we define $\dim _\delta (T)$ as the supremum of the $\delta $-dimensions of the irreducible components of $T$. If $Z$ is a closed subspace of $X$, then we set $\dim _\delta (Z) = \dim _\delta (|Z|)$. </p>
</article>